---
code: records-torn-line
when-fires: a line that looks like ours carried no terminal token, so it lost its terminating write. plan/records.rs admit_records (the strict admission path); the forgiving deframer emits it too. `{count}` is what was seen before the walk stopped.
why: 262 §1 pin-late-and-alien-records: the tear is DETECTED rather than parsed, which is what keeps a truncated coordinate from reading as a valid shorter one.
---
-- book.sh --
#!/bin/sh
hork tune --profile web

-- probe-results.txt --
dorc-records/1 nonce=dorc attempt=1 host=localhost book=6b796e0c816aa119a94373a3ab99578a69820f243017ce833973242dd6f9a79e sites=0 @@dorc@@
dorc site 0 effect=holds rc=0
dorc-records-end/1 nonce=dorc @@dorc@@

-- replay --
$ dorc plan --book=book.sh --results - < probe-results.txt > /dev/null
records: warning[records-torn-line]: sm 1 torn (no terminal token) record
line(s) discarded (counted, never folded)

$ dorc-loom --this vars
case: records-torn-line
{{count}} = "1"
